{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454684-v5-backgrounds-and-how-they-appear-on-a-character-sheet","id":1454684,"title":"V5: Backgrounds and how they appear on a character sheet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-11T06:53:33-07:00","id":1454684,"title":"V5: Backgrounds and how they appear on a character sheet","content":"Hi everyone!! I recently had someone talk with me about backgrounds for V5 and how they should appear on the character sheet. I made an alternative sheet for them with a different layout for the background section, but they way they've been discussing it with me is starting to me make me question if the layout for backgrounds on my V5 sheets is right or not. So, I wanted to discuss it with y'all to get your take on the subject.<br /> <br /> So, my original idea for the backgrounds section, and the way it appears currently on my sheets, is to list the background and the rating, and then you have 8 blank lines under it to expand out any info you want to want to write about the background. So, in my mind (in relation to all my past edition Vampire sheets), it's a combo between the background section and the expanded backgrounds section, that way they're all listed together. If that makes sense... So, if you had Contacts 2, you'd write that out with the dot rating, then list some info about the contact. I have 10 spots to record backgrounds in this way.<br /> <br /> The guy I've been talking to says that backgrounds don't really work that way in V5 anymore, and he asked me to re-work the backgrounds section. He had me flip the layout, so you have a blank line up top and then 8 lines with dots. He says this better represents how backgrounds work. An example he gave me he says you have the background &quot;DJ Job&quot; and lists out Fame (listeners) 2, Resources (wage) 1, Status (station) 2, Contacts (station crew)3, and Contacts (management) 1. That would fit in one of the 10 spots I have in the backgrounds section. He says then if your character became a Harpy(for example) you'd write another section in a similar manner.<br /> <br /> My question is this: Is that the way backgrounds work in V5? I might be too ingrained in the way the older versions of Vampire work, but I'm not quite understanding this. I mean, I get he's listing background related to a characters concept or job but I'm not seeing where you'd be able to do that enough to fill out ten spots on a character sheet like that. In my mind, it's seems you'd list out the backgrounds your character has, and then have a little room to write some info related to that background. But anyway, is that even the proper way to do backgrounds in V5 and is the way he's suggesting the proper way? I know there are a few backgrounds that work in a similar manner, like Haven, where you list out some traits related to that Haven, but I didn't think that backgrounds in general worked like that.<br /> <br /> If the layout of backgrounds on my character sheets isn't correct, I can go back and fix them all, but I didn't want to do all that work if the current layout is fine. So, I wanted to get some thoughts and opinions before I did anything. What do y'all think?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for the discussion!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":24,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","user":"Mr Gone","date":". 07-11-2021, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T04:12:30-07:00","id":1454809,"title":"","content":"The rulebook does not clarify that a lot IRC, but the way NPCs are presented in Onyx Path books is as this guy is telling you. I use the backgrounds the same way as described, I use a line for the concept name, 4-5 lines for further description and then all the backgrounds tied to that concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25915-nicolai","name":"nicolai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T15:55:40-07:00","id":1455049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nicolai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454684-v5-backgrounds-and-how-they-appear-on-a-character-sheet?p=1454809#post1454809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rulebook does not clarify that a lot IRC, but the way NPCs are presented in Onyx Path books is as this guy is telling you. I use the backgrounds the same way as described, I use a line for the concept name, 4-5 lines for further description and then all the backgrounds tied to that concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I had some discussions about it over on a Facebook post about it, and some use it the way I presented, and some liked the other way.<br /> <br /> So, I'm glad I have some options for people. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Appreciate you chiming in too! Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T23:25:50-07:00","id":1455065,"title":"","content":"I've looked in the books, and Backgrounds seem to be grouped like that just for ease of finding info. I don't think it's supposed to be a blanket formatting thing. But whatever people prefer, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments"